    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (especially when sentiment is neutral or negative).",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if sentiment turns negative (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00) and recent prices show downward momentum.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10% for next period.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is positive (e.g., 0.50) and price is trending upward — avoid overconfidence.",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is below forecast by >10% for 3+ consecutive days, reduce next forecast by 5-10%.",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term sentiment shifts — smooth transitions between sentiment states (e.g., 0.00 → 0.50) with gradual adjustments."
